Clear a wedged instance from the launcher, so the icon works without rebuilding
the editor.

The shortcut points at the projicons launcher, not at editors.exe. The real fix
for the dead-icon bug lives in editors.exe (see
single-instance-launch-wedge.patch), but that binary needs a full core/CEF
build. The launcher builds standalone against Qt plus Windows system libraries,
so it is the one piece that can ship the recovery immediately.

ClearWedgedInstance() runs just before editors.exe is started. It reads
APP_MUTEX_NAME from the editor's own defines.h rather than repeating it, because
a second copy of APP_USER_MODEL_ID in ProjIcons.pro drifting from defines.h is
exactly what previously made PW Docs share a taskbar button with its siblings.

Two rules keep it safe:
  - if any process from this install still shows a window, nothing is touched;
    a live editor must never be killed, even when busy and briefly not
    answering;
  - a process younger than 90 seconds is left alone, so double-clicking the
    icon cannot kill the instance that is still coming up.

Only this install's own editors.exe / editors_helper.exe are considered, so the
other PW apps are never affected. common.pri also gains -luser32 (EnumWindows,
IsWindowVisible, GetWindowThreadProcessId) and the include paths for src and
src/prop.

Apply to: desktop-apps/win-linux/extras/projicons/src/main.cpp
          desktop-apps/win-linux/extras/projicons/common.pri
